<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baloch people</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baloch">Baloch</a> are an Iranian-speaking people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balochistan">Balochistan</a>, a region divided between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, who speak the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balochi-language">Balochi language</a>. Organised in tribes under hereditary chiefs, many migrated over the centuries into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a>, where Baloch families such as the Talpurs rose to power. The Khanate of Kalat united many Baloch tribes from the 17th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baloch-people.jpg" alt="Baloch people" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mostafameraji · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Baloch_people_(8).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
